      "note": "Anchor: 0xfdb93e00f3b1d24303db7f43eaa5ef50d3fde957ddeec7c0feb8c5497ba11182, block 22881853 index 294, timestamp 1752066815, receipt status 0x1. I re-anchored the record. Walking the attacker EOA 0x0a652decf9caca373e2b50607ecb7b069d71a7ba's 75 transactions and tracing each candidate with callTracer, the six transactions at blocks 22864513-22864829 touch the ZKSwap L1 contract but never reach the verifier (0 frames at 0x961369d3), while 0xfdb93e00 at block 22881853 is the first successful transaction whose trace contains STATICCALL 0x8eca806a -> 0x961369d347ef7a6896bdd39cbe2b89e3911f521f -> DELEGATECALL 0xd12f4d8329584f36aed67f807f42d9a02beb9534. A second single-exit proof followed at 22881898 and the first drain, 10,000 USDT, at 22882059, all before the previously recorded anchor 0x5488f6bb at 22882195, which proves fifteen exits in one call. The old anchor is retained as a source; verification.legacy.reanchored is set. Defect, reproduced from the trace rather than from source (the implementation is unverified on Etherscan): the exit path 0xd6973fc6 on the L1 contract reaches VerifierExit through three delegatecall hops and STATICCALLs the verifier proxy with selector 0xc81a27ad and 708 bytes of calldata. In every one of the 15 frames of 0x5488f6bb and the single frames of 0xfdb93e00 and 0x3e47cdb5, the implementation frame consumes exactly 1,496 gas, makes zero sub-calls and returns 0x...01. A Groth16 or PLONK verification of a 708-byte proof cannot run in 1,496 gas and cannot avoid calling the bn256 pairing precompile at 0x08; the absence of any child frame is direct onchain proof that no verification is performed and the function returns true unconditionally, matching the published VerifierExit.sol in l2labs/zkswap-contracts. This is a logic defect in deployed EVM code, not a compromised or misconfigured verification key: a wrong key would still run the pairing check and consume hundreds of thousands of gas, and there is no parameter of this contract at which the deployed body becomes correct because it contains no verification logic to parameterise. Target and code history: execution context is the VerifierExit proxy 0x961369d347ef7a6896bdd39cbe2b89e3911f521f, relationship proxy, artifact 0xd12f4d8329584f36aed67f807f42d9a02beb9534. eth_getCode on the artifact hashes to 0x6598e055c93c3f1f4d1109ef77ec5008185badb18d8a2fe8250a70e32d65f5a0 at both the proxy creation block 11841962 and block 22881852. proxy.getTarget() returns 0xd12f4d83 at blocks 11841962, 15000000, 20000000 and 22881852. eth_getLogs over the proxy from 11841962 to 22881852 returns zero logs, and eth_getLogs over the UpgradeGatekeeper 0x714b2d10210f2a3a7aa614f949259c87613689ab over the same range returns five logs, all in the creation block and none of them UpgradeComplete (0xfce1ab62ee865fe697bab8ed88a303d0d9a2bef9ef20f74822b755fe89a03985). The implementation was therefore never changed. Code age 1752066815 - 1613135194 = 138,931,621 s (1608.00 days); the previous anchor gave 138,935,773 s. Loss: rebuilt from receipts. All 44 transactions that move value out of the L1 contract are listed in source-7; netting the contract's ERC20 Transfer logs between blocks 22882059 and 22885419 and adding its one outgoing internal transfer of 362.365589999999975424 ETH gives 31 components. The largest are 29.99136703 WBTC (3,276,346.91 USD), 362.365589999999975424 ETH (964,214.97 USD), 275,044.680955 USDT, 86,796.815421 USDC and 608.630632806629553005 AAVE (182,522.24 USD). Three fabricated ZKS tokens were deposited in the same transactions and net to exactly zero, so they are excluded as attacker-supplied inputs; gZKS, the real ZKS token and the wrapped-QTUM ERC20 have no DefiLlama series and carry quantity only. Priced components total 4,867,767.04 USD against the 5 million USD Blockaid reported. Four attacker-controlled recipients appear across the drain: 0x728001a8, 0x2d3103c8, 0x62b22373 and 0x6c0ce5df, the last two funded by a second EOA 0x23746176db73fca77e3961e75a9bbc51539ee1d1; all are recorded as attacker addresses and the whole sequence is one campaign against one execution context."
